new file mode 100644
index 000000000..2e204166d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/2482-mach3-post.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+## #2482 - Mach3 Mill post (3-axis)
+
+Sources: the public "Using Mach3Mill" manual (the G-code and M-code lists
+and the General Config notes), behaviour only, and RS-274 / ISO 6983 for
+the shared words. The script is derived from our own `grblhal.cps`. No
+vendor post or vendor output was consulted.
+
+- **Decided: tool change is `T<n> M6`, then `G43 H<n>`.** Z goes up first.
+  **Why:** Mach3 keeps a tool table, and M6 runs the user's M6Start /
+  M6End macros (a manual stop, a tool setter or an ATC). The post cannot
+  know what the macro does, so it lifts Z before it.
+- **Decided: canned cycles G73, G81, G82, G83, G85, G86, G89 with G98.**
+  Mach3 lists these cycles. A dwell P on G82, G86 and G89 is in seconds.
+  A G83 dwell is refused by name, because G83 has no P word in the list.
+- **Decided: the dwell unit is a post option (`dwellInMilliseconds`, off by
+  default).** **Why:** Mach3 has the General Config setting "G04 Dwell
+  param in ms". The post cannot read the control's setting, so the user
+  states it. Off writes seconds.
+- **Decided: G41/G42, G84 tapping and probing are refused by name.** Mach3
+  has G41/G42, but they depend on the control's tool table radius, which
+  the post does not know. Tapping and probing depend on the user's
+  machine setup and macros.
+- **Decided: G91.1 in the header.** Arc centres are incremental, stated
+  every time. Mach3's IJ mode is a setting, so the post never assumes it.
+- **No own machine.** A Mach3 user picks an existing 3-axis machine (for
+  example "VMC 3-axis") and edits the limits.
+
+Not exercised: no reading on a real Mach3 control. That Mach3 accepts
+G91.1 is from the manual's word list only, not tested on a control.
+
+Cost to change later: low. The script is one asset and one registry line.

From 7a44d6fa43308cbe1dbbb8f1ebf0ca8a43beddb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:47:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(post): route mach3 header notes through onComment and
 count 21 posts

Main's PR #3087 (issue #2996) routes post header notes through the JS
onComment hook, and every shipped post overrides it. The merge refresh of
this PR with main failed the comment_escape header-notes test because the
new mach3.cps had no override, so raw English text landed in the NC output,
and because its shipped-post count asserted 20 while the branch now ships
21. This adds the mach3 onComment override, in the form the other posts
use, and sets the count to 21.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 assets/posts/mach3.cps              | 2 ++
 crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/assets/posts/mach3.cps b/assets/posts/mach3.cps
index 1c05a58bd..1f8b7b51b 100644
--- a/assets/posts/mach3.cps
+++ b/assets/posts/mach3.cps
@@ -282,6 +282,8 @@ function joinDash(parts) {  // the non-empty parts, " - " between
 // so user text stays inert.
 var ACTIVE = /^\s*(MSG|DEBUG|PRINT|LOG|LOGOPEN|LOGAPPEND|LOGCLOSE|PROBEOPEN|PROBECLOSE|ABORT|AXIS|PY|PYRUN)\b/i;
 function note(s) { block(["(" + (ACTIVE.test(s) ? "- " + s : s) + ")"]); }
+// Program notes use this dialect without truncating the stated bound.
+function onComment(s) { note(commentText(s)); }
 function commentParam(name, value) {
   if (name === "SetupName") setupName = clean(value);
   else if (name === "OperationName") opName = clean(value);
diff --git a/crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs b/crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs
index 621a7440c..b08b7611b 100644
--- a/crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs
+++ b/crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs
@@ -305,5 +305,5 @@ fn header_notes_use_each_shipped_dialect_and_keep_the_full_surface_bound() {
         }
         seen += 1;
     }
-    assert_eq!(seen, 20, "every shipped post is checked");
+    assert_eq!(seen, 21, "every shipped post is checked");
 }

